Z||000000||SilverFieroV6||05-22-2001||12:55 AM||||The 86 came home today after the clutch was replaced.  This is the first I have driven the car since I bought it last week.  I thought the car was in pretty good shape, but either I was way wrong or I have a bad idea of what pretty good shape is.<BR>List of problems minor and semi major<BR>1. Needs brakes<BR>2.head light door is busted so it is in the up position.<BR>3.Gas guage has no friggin clue how much gas is in the car(goes from empty to full then back to empty in matter of secconds, even when the car is stoped) <BR>4. I belive there to be a small electricial problem. (will explain more in detail below as I need some opinions/help/advice it may be a major problem)<BR>5. needs an o2 sensor<BR>6.  small oil leak but big enough that you can smell it while driveing down the road<BR>7. needles in the console(thermostat) have fallen off and laying at the bottom of there little box<BR>8.needs a new lock for the driver side door (so messed up the key cant even get in the lock,  looks as someone tried to pick it or drill it)<BR>9.  Small exhaust leak<P>OK the electricail problem may be something pretty small im not sure.  I first noticed  it when i went to pick up the car it was raining lightly, i turned on the windshield wipers and nothing not even a sound.  I made it a few minutes down the road back to my house.  I started to look for the fuse box and noticed there was three or four empty slots (one being the wipers).   I also noticed there was two empty boxes that are to carry spare fuses.  I think thats a bad sign.  I replaced the fuses that were missing and now the wipers work  but wont turn off (the cruise still doesnt work) and the radio only works when it wants to.  I can get in the car and start it one time and the radio is on fine   but then the next time it doesnt make a peep (but appears to be on)  I took the car out aroung the block ttrying to see what all was wrong with it  and noticed that when i put on the blinker the batter guauge (next to the oil pressure in the 86 and up)  goes down when the blinker lights up and goes back up when it goes off.   When the radio does work the battery guage is about two notches before the redline (as in to much)  when it doesnt work it is five or six notches down from the redline.  <P>Ok anyone ever have any type of trouble like this and if so what was the cause.   i basically have no money for repiars so doing this right the first time is a good thing as the money i had went for the clutch.  <BR>Thanks for all the help <BR>Sam Clark<P><BR>{edit} one last question{edit}<P>I found this in the car and was wondering if anyone knoes if it is the e-brake cable or the clutch cable. Its the packageing it came in  I have a part # and a semi name to it.<BR>prt#    1#10042386<P>says on it    "cable ASM"   <P>thanks again <BR>Sam Clark<BR><p>[This message has been edited by SilverFieroV6 (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||10:03 AM||||it sounds like there is a bad connector somewhere in the wireing that includes the voltmeter. I really doubt your battery voltage is dropping that much when you put on a turn signal or the radio, but if a connector is shared by the radio and the meter, then it could be dirty or the wire could be about to break - so that when there is current flowing through it you see a big voltage drop across the bad conenction.||||reg||1
